{
 "sheet": 1,
 "name": "IR2153STRPBF",
 "kind": "motor_driver",
 "manufacturer": "Infineon (International Rectifier)",
 "title": "Self-oscillating 600 V half-bridge gate driver with 555-type oscillator",
 "source": {
  "document": "Data Sheet No. PD60062",
  "revision": "revP",
  "pages": 9
 },
 "summary": "A half-bridge gate driver with its own RC oscillator: one resistor and one capacitor set the frequency, and the low-side and high-side outputs alternate at 50 % duty with about 1.2 µs of deadtime between them. The high side floats on an offset of up to 600 V, VCC has a 15.6 V internal zener clamp and a 75 µA start-up current, and pulling the CT pin low shuts both outputs off. The IR2153 (DIP) and IR2153S (SOIC) need an outside bootstrap diode; the IR2153D (DIP only) has one inside.",
