   "title": "Typical connection, IR2153 and IR2153S",
   "page": 1,
   "description": "Self-oscillating half bridge of two N-channel MOSFETs on a rail of up to 600 V. R1 trickles current from the rail into VCC, where C1 holds it and the internal zener clamps it. RT from the RT pin to CT and the capacitor CT from CT to COM set the switching frequency. An external diode from VCC to VB charges the bootstrap capacitor C2 while Q2 is on. HO and LO drive the gates through R2 and R3, and the midpoint feeds an inductive load through C3, returning to COM. Turning Q3 on pulls CT to COM and stops both outputs.",
